[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5082757553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121768#issuecomment-5082757553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121768","id":5082757553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLvS5sQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T08:41:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T08:41:13Z","body":"In what way is this a bug? This is expected behavior I would say, nowhere does it say that inner classes do not conflict with global classes (hence why there is an error there)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5082757553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084033165","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121768#issuecomment-5084033165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121768","id":5084033165,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLwgwjQ","user":{"login":"Raildex","id":14938934,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTM4OTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14938934?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex","html_url":"https://github.com/Raildex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raildex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T15:00:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:00:50Z","body":"We do not have namespaces. If this is not a bug but a design choice, GDScript needs namespaces, or any other mechanism to avoid such issues.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084033165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084184663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121768#issuecomment-5084184663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121768","id":5084184663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLwqAVw","user":{"login":"Essler","id":4809932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDk5MzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4809932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler","html_url":"https://github.com/Essler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Essler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T15:42:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:42:31Z","body":"Implementing a namespacing solution in GDScript would be a departure from Godot's design philosophy. Keeping things simple and approachable is key. Imagine a new developer having to resolve namespace issues like you do in Java or C#.\n\nIdeally, plugin authors would avoid using common names for their classes, but since they don't, devs just have to use more specific class names.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084184663/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5331323368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121768#issuecomment-5331323368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121768","id":5331323368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPcWJ6A","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T16:47:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T16:47:12Z","body":"I'd have to check how GDScript currently handles this behavior, but intuitively my thought here would be that `OuterClass.InnerClass` should work everywhere, and `InnerClass` alone should work inside of `OuterClass` as long as it doesn't conflict with an outer class name. So my expectations would be:\n\n```gdscript\n# settings.gd\nextends Node\nclass_name Settings\n\n...\n```\n\n```gdscript\n# foo.gd\nextends Node\nclass_name Foo\n\nclass Settings: # (I would expect) No error here\n\tvar foo: int = 0\n\nclass OtherStuff:\n\tvar num: int = 1\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t# Creates an instance of the class defined by settings.gd since global classes take precedence\n\tvar settings = Settings.new()\n\n\t# Creates an instance of the inner class Settings up above since the outer class is explicitly stated\n\tvar inner_settings = Foo.Settings.new()\n\n\t# Creates an instance of inner class OtherStuff up above since no global class takes this name\n\tvar stuff = OtherStuff.new()\n```\n\n```gdscript\n# third_class.gd\nextends Node\nclass_name ThirdClass\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t# Could error because of no global class named OtherStuff, or could infer that the only class named OtherStuff\n\t# is Foo.OtherStuff\n\tvar stuff = OtherStuff.new()\n\n\t# Creates an instance of Foo's inner classes since they are explicitly stated to belong to Foo\n\tvar foo_settings = Foo.Settings.new()\n\tvar foo_stuff = Foo.OtherStuff.new()\n\n\t# Creates an instance of the class defined by settings.gd since global class is implied\n\tvar settings  = Settings.new()\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5331323368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]